            <ArticleTitle>Gender differences in coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>340-51; quiz 352-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery disease in women is associated with higher morbidity and mortality than in men. The purpose of this article is to summarize recent literature concerning gender-based differences. Specific differences in pathophysiology, traditional and psychosocial risk factors, symptom presentation, treatments, and outcomes between women and men will be reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
